## Pointers

### Pointer Basics

```c
// Pointer declaration
int *ptr;                      // Pointer to int
char *ch_ptr;                  // Pointer to char
int **ptr_to_ptr;              // Pointer to pointer

// Address-of operator (&)
int x = 10;
int *ptr = &x;                 // ptr points to x
printf("%p\n", ptr);           // Prints address (e.g., 0x7fff5fbff8ac)

// Dereference operator (*)
printf("%d\n", *ptr);          // 10 (value at address)
*ptr = 20;                     // x is now 20
```

**Visual Example:**
```
Variable x:
┌────┬────────┐
│ x  │   10   │  <- value
└────┴────────┘
  ^
  │
  └── Address: 0x1000

Pointer ptr:
┌──────┬──────────────┐
│ ptr  │ 0x1000       │  <- address of x
└──────┴──────────────┘
  ^
  │
  └── Address: 0x2000

int *ptr = &x;
printf("%d\n", *ptr);          // Dereference: prints 10
printf("%p\n", ptr);           // Address: prints 0x1000
printf("%p\n", &ptr);          // Address of pointer: prints 0x2000
```

### Pointers & Arrays

```c
int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

// Array name decays to pointer to first element
int *ptr = arr;                // Same as &arr[0]

// Pointer arithmetic
printf("%d\n", *ptr);          // 10 (first element)
printf("%d\n", *(ptr + 1));    // 20 (second element)
printf("%d\n", ptr[2]);        // 30 (array notation)

// Iterate with pointer
for (int *p = arr; p < arr + 5; p++) {
    printf("%d ", *p);         // 10 20 30 40 50
}

