### Q19: Compare hash table vs binary search tree
```
Operation          Hash Table  BST       Binary Search
Insert             O(1) avg    O(log n)  N/A
Search             O(1) avg    O(log n)  O(log n) sorted array
Delete             O(1) avg    O(log n)  N/A
Range query        O(n)        O(k+log n) O(log n)
Worst case search  O(n)        O(n)      O(log n)
Memory overhead    High        Low       None
```

**Implementation:**
```c
// Simple hash table
#define HASH_SIZE 100

typedef struct {
    char *key;
    int value;
} HashEntry;

typedef struct {
    HashEntry *entries[HASH_SIZE];
} HashTable;

int hash_function(const char *key) {
    int hash = 0;
    for (int i = 0; key[i]; i++) {
        hash = (hash * 31 + key[i]) % HASH_SIZE;
    }
    return hash;
}

void hash_insert(HashTable *ht, const char *key, int value) {
    int index = hash_function(key);
    // Handle collisions (chaining or probing)
    ht->entries[index]->value = value;
}

int hash_search(HashTable *ht, const char *key) {
    int index = hash_function(key);
    if (ht->entries[index]) {
        return ht->entries[index]->value;
    }
    return -1;
}
```

